Release 0.5.1: the sidebar folds into a menu on phones

On a phone the sidebar's links scrolled sideways in a row, so sections
past the edge of the screen, the current one among them, were out of
sight. Under md it's now a bar with the current section's name and a
menu button, as the site header has; the sections and the foot drop
below it, one per row. Details are in CHANGELOG.md under 0.5.1.

## Fixed

- Sidebar: under md, a bar with the current section's name and a menu
  button (js/sidebar.js); the nav and the foot, wrapped in
  `.al-sidebar__menu`, show only while it's open. Escape closes it and
  returns focus; choosing a link closes it. Every name shows in the
  menu, collapsed or not, and Collapse is hidden. New classes:
  `.al-sidebar__bar`, `.al-sidebar__here`, `.al-sidebar__toggle`,
  `.al-sidebar__menu`; React `Shell` gains `menuId`.
- js/nav-menu.js (`wireNavMenu()`): the menu button's behaviour, now
  shared by the sidebar and the site header.
- The showcase's introduction: built by Arabesque Labs to set the
  standard for its products, in one plain sentence, without the
  highlights; the Arabic follows.
- Specs (English and Arabic), the READMEs' list of helpers, and the
  sidebar example; check-page tests the menu on a phone and the sidebar
  above md.

